init writes one Project Specification TOML to --out. It does not discover a
default path, does not prompt, and does not generate a project. Destination
must not already exist (no overwrite).

Required: --out, --name, --module. Optional: --archetype (cli|tui, default cli),
--description, --destination (default ./<name>), --visibility (private|public),
--profile (repeatable; only "distribution" is selectable today).

The written file is validated with the same field contract as validate before
it is written. Next step: foundry validate --spec <out> && foundry plan …

Examples:
  foundry init --out ./my-cli.toml --name my-cli --module github.com/you/my-cli
  foundry init --out ./app.toml --name app --module github.com/you/app --archetype tui
  foundry init --out ./pub.toml --name pub --module github.com/you/pub \
    --visibility public --profile distribution

Usage:
  foundry init [flags]

Flags:
      --archetype string      archetype: cli|tui (default "cli")
      --description string    one-line description (default: derived from name)
      --destination string    generate destination (default: ./<name>)
  -h, --help                  help for init
      --module string         Go module path (final segment must equal name; required)
      --name string           project name (kebab-case; required)
      --out string            path to write the Project Spec TOML (required; must not exist)
      --profile stringArray   optional profile id (repeatable; distribution only today)
      --visibility string     visibility: private|public (default "private")

Global Flags:
      --color string    color mode: auto|always|never (text mode only) (default "auto")
      --output string   output mode: text|json (default "text")
      --quiet           suppress non-essential human output (text mode only)
      --verbose         diagnostic detail on stderr (text mode only)
